⚠️ Potential issue | 🔴 Critical

CRITICAL: Script has CRLF line endings and will not execute on Unix/Linux systems.

The static analysis detected literal carriage returns (SC1017) on every line. The script file has Windows line endings (CRLF) instead of Unix line endings (LF). This will cause /bin/bash: /path/to/verify.sh: No such file or directory errors on Linux/macOS when executed.

Fix by converting line endings:

dos2unix verify.sh
# OR
sed -i 's/\r$//' verify.sh
# OR
tr -d '\r' < verify.sh > verify.sh.tmp && mv verify.sh.tmp verify.sh
Alternatively, ensure the file is committed with .gitattributes enforcing LF for shell scripts:

*.sh text eol=lf
